# L §4.3 rule 2: "an input whose rows all govern always ... is read without [a law date], by a def as by a move"; and an
# ask line that reads one directly needs no law either (only "a law-dated input or band" needs one, L §4.3). x's row
# governs always: q1 = 1, q2 = y + 1 = 3. (Writer 6.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input x: int
input y: int

def z: int = y + 1

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  x = 1 governs always "s"
  y = 2 governs always "s"

ask q1: x
ask q2: z
=== expect
q1: 1
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: 3
  cut 2026-12-31
